Step 1 — Purchase Request 

Created By: EMPLOYEE 
  

Status Flow: 

SUBMITTED 
    ↓ 
APPROVED or REJECTED 
  

Purpose:Employee requests goods/services. 
 Example: 

2 Laptops 
5 Mouse 
  

Step 2 — Approval 

Performed By: MANAGER 
  

Actions: Approve or Reject 
 Manager adds: managerComment 
  

Step 3 — Vendor Management 

Performed By: PURCHASE_TEAM 
  

Vendor contains: 

vendorCode 
companyName 
contactPerson 
email 
phone 
address 
 

Purpose: Maintain supplier database. 
  

Step 4 — RFQ (Request For Quotation) 

Created By: PURCHASE_TEAM 
  

Created Against: APPROVED PR 
  

Business Rule: Only APPROVED PR can create RFQ. 
  

RFQ Status Flow: 

DRAFT 
   ↓ 
ISSUED 
   ↓ 
CLOSED 
  

Meaning: 

DRAFT 

RFQ created but not sent. 

ISSUED 

RFQ sent to vendors. 

CLOSED 

Quotation collection completed. 

 

Step 5 — Quotation 

Created By: PURCHASE_TEAM 
  

(Manually enters vendor quotations received offline) 

Contains: 

Vendor 
Items 
Unit Price 
Total Price 
Total Amount 
  

Business Rules: 

RFQ must be ISSUED 
 
Vendor must belong to RFQ 
 
One Vendor = One Quotation Per RFQ 
 
totalPrice auto-calculated 
 
totalAmount auto-calculated 
  

Quotation Status Flow: 

SUBMITTED 
      ↓ 
SELECTED 
or 
REJECTED 
  

Meaning: 

SUBMITTED 

Quotation received. 

SELECTED 

Vendor won the RFQ. 

REJECTED 

Vendor lost the RFQ. 

 

4. QUOTATION COMPARISON 

Purpose: Compare quotations for same RFQ. 
  

System Behavior: Sort quotations by totalAmount ascending. 
  

Example: 

Vendor A = 95,000 
 
Vendor B = 90,000 
 
Vendor C = 100,000 
  

Result: 

Rank 1 → Vendor B 
 
Rank 2 → Vendor A 
 
Rank 3 → Vendor C 
  

Important: 

System suggests lowest quotation. 
 
Purchase Team can choose any vendor. 
  

 

5. VENDOR SELECTION 

Performed By: PURCHASE_TEAM 
  

Rule: RFQ must be CLOSED 
  

Selection Flow: 

Choose Quotation 
      ↓ 
Selected Quotation 
      ↓ 
Status = SELECTED 
      ↓ 
All Others = REJECTED 
  

Rule: 

Only one quotation can be selected. 
  

6. PURCHASE ORDER 

Created By: PURCHASE_TEAM 
 Source: SELECTED QUOTATION 
  

Business Rules: 

Quotation must be SELECTED 
 
One quotation = One PO 
 
Duplicate PO not allowed 
  

Data copied from quotation: 

Vendor 
 
Items 
 
Unit Price 
 
Total Amount 
  

Purpose: Official order sent to vendor. 
  

Purchase Order Status Flow 

DRAFT 
   ↓ 
ISSUED 
   ↓ 
CANCELLED 
  

Meaning: 

DRAFT 

PO generated but not sent. 

ISSUED 

PO sent to vendor. 

CANCELLED 

PO cancelled. 

